<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="59938" href="schedule/2012/fall/NRES/512/59938.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2012" href="schedule/2012.xml">2012</calendarYear><term id="120128" href="schedule/2012/fall.xml">Fall 2012</term><subject id="NRES" href="schedule/2012/fall/NRES.xml">Natural Resources and Environmental Sciences</subject><course id="512" href="schedule/2012/fall/NRES/512.xml">Discussions in NRES</course></parents><sectionNumber>WQ </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Special Topics-Water Quality</sectionTitle><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course will bring students up-to-date on current water quality research with particular emphasis on issues relevant to Illinois. Experts from agencies such as the Illinois Environmental Protection Agency, the U.S. Geological Survey, the U of I, and other universities will make presentations on water quality topics during some of the class meetings. These talks and current scientific literature will then serve as a basis for student led discussions and presentations.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2012-08-27Z</startDate><endDate>2012-12-12Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="CNF">Conference</type><start>04:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>M      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>N527</roomNumber><buildingName>Turner Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="David" firstName="M">David, M</instructor><instructor lastName="Johnson" firstName="T">Johnson, T</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>